  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--blue">Monday to Friday</p>
      <h2>A Lower Secondary day</h2>
      <p class="lede">The core subjects first, then History or Executive Function. Afternoons are for making, moving and experiments.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt">{% set dayKey = "lower-secondary" %}{% include "partials/dayline.njk" %}</div>
  </div>
</section>
{% set waveColor = "white" %}{% include "partials/wave.njk" %}

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Beyond the core</p>
      <h2>Where it gets built</h2>
      <p class="lede">Specialist and vocational classes, in English, with the tools out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cards cards--3 mt">
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("flask", "blue") }}<h3>Art of Science</h3><p>Experiments that use the morning's science.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("tools", "sun") }}<h3>Maker Space</h3><p>Technology and design. Tools, materials and a problem: students design, build, test and present.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("ball", "green") }}<h3>Movement</h3><p>Sport and fitness.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("heart", "coral") }}<h3>Wellbeing</h3><p>A class on the things that make the rest of the week go better.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("clock", "violet") }}<h3>Review</h3><p>Time to catch up and ask the question you did not ask in class.</p></div>
      <div class="card">{{ ic.icon("book", "green") }}<h3>History and Executive Function</h3><p>Late morning, before lunch. The past, and the habits that get work done: planning, organising, finishing.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="center mt"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ '/families/schedule/#lower-secondary' | url }}">See the week at a glance</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap two">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--blue">Executive Function</p>
      <h2>The habits that get work done</h2>
      <p>A timetabled class, late morning, alternating with History. It is about the part of school nobody teaches directly: planning a piece of work, breaking it up, keeping track of it, and finishing it.</p>
      <p>Some of it is routine — packing the right kit, knowing what a lesson needs before it starts. So one of last year's tasks was to make the reminders the classroom actually uses — what to put on before a practical, what to bring to sport — and they are still on the wall.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      {% set collagePhotos = ["poster-lab-safety", "poster-sport-kit"] %}
      {% set collageArt = true %}
      {% set collageCredit = "Made by our <strong>Lower Secondary</strong> students in Executive Function." %}
      {% include "partials/collage.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

